<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of OECD French forecasts by full year.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of OECD French forecasts by full year.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development gave the following economic forecasts in its latest report on France. (Percentage change, seasonally adjusted annual rates, 1980 prices.</p>
<p>    Category		     1996     1997     1998</p>
<p> Private consumption	    2.4	1.7	2.4</p>
<p> Government consumption	 1.6	1.1	1.0</p>
<p> Total investment		 0.6	2.5	3.4</p>
<p>  of which government	  -2.5     -0.2	0.0</p>
<p>	     households	   1.5	2.3	3.3</p>
<p>	     business	     1.1	3.4	4.5</p>
<p> Stockbuilding		   -1.0	0.5	0.2</p>
<p> Total domestic demand	  0.9	2.3	2.6</p>
<p> Exports			    2.4	5.8	6.4</p>
<p> Imports			    1.1	5.3	6.3</p>
<p> Foreign balance		  0.4	0.2	0.1</p>
<p> GDP				  1.3	2.5	2.6</p>
<p> Employment			 0.0	0.3	0.8</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	     12.4     12.5     12.1</p>
<p> Household saving ratio	12.7     12.6     12.4</p>
<p> Private consumption deflator 1.8	1.3	1.2</p>
<p> Inflation (GDP deflator)     1.7	1.3	1.4</p>
<p> Short-term interest rates    3.9	3.3	3.8</p>
<p> Long-Term interest rates     6.6	6.1	6.3</p>
<p>General government borrowing</p>
<p>    requirement		  -4.1     -3.2     -3.0</p>
<p> Current balance		  1.3	1.5	1.6</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
